    "body": "It's not me who says it, it's the validator!\nDid you try https://validator.w3.org/nu/#textarea\n\nHey, just look at the code. Not only <hgroup> error, what you think about this line(!) : <p>Living Standard — Last Updated 19 October 2015<p>\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-hgroup-element\nHTML Standard<https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-hgroup-element>\nTypically, the address element would be included along with other information in a footer element.. The contact information for a node node is a collection of address elements defined by the first applicable entry from the following list:. If node is an article element If node is a body element. The contact information consists of all the address elements that have node as an ancestor and do ...\nhtml.spec.whatwg.org\n\n\n\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"\">\n    <meta name=\"author\" content=\"Whatgw\">\n    <title>W3C error · WhatWG</title>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <header>\n     <hgroup>\n      <h1>Fullscreen API</h1>\n      == > W3C ERROR with that line <p>Living Standard — Last Updated 19 October 2015<p>\n     </hgroup>\n     <dl>\n      <dt>Participate:</dt>\n      <dd><a href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/fullscreen\">GitHub whatwg/fullscreen</a></dd>\n      <dt>Commits:</dt>\n      <dd><a href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/fullscreen/commits\">GitHub whatwg/fullscreen/commits</a></dd>\n     </dl>\n    </header>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n<p> tag must go after <h6> with <hgroup>!\n\nAnyways, it's W3C fist!\n\n[cid:980725c9-6f6c-47c0-85c9-3dfd571d99e6]\n\n________________________________\nDe : Domenic Denicola ***@***.***>\nEnvoyé : 26 octobre 2022 21:54\nÀ : whatwg/html ***@***.***>\nCc : Oznogco ***@***.***>; Author ***@***.***>\nObjet : Re: [whatwg/html] \"Here are some examples of valid headings contai...\" (Issue #8438)\n\n\nThat's incorrect; they are valid according to the spec.\n\n—\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub<https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8438#issuecomment-1292861843>, or unsubscribe<https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AG3ZPWFTDWNJGMEUBFAW4U3WFHOGLANCNFSM6AAAAAARPPI4CU>.\nYou are receiving this because you authored the thread.Message ID: ***@***.***>\n",
