    "body": "Thanks for the precision,\n\nI know that the validator has some problems, moreover he must have received a large number of complaints after October 5th. Because they changed some warnings to replace them with \"info\".\n\nP.S. 4.3.8 The header element, the <p> at the end is useless or must be closed...\n\n<p>Living Standard — Last Updated 19 October 2015<p>\n\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-header-element\n\nHTML Standard<https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-header-element>\nTypically, the address element would be included along with other information in a footer element.. The contact information for a node node is a collection of address elements defined by the first applicable entry from the following list:. If node is an article element If node is a body element. The contact information consists of all the address elements that have node as an ancestor and do ...\nhtml.spec.whatwg.org\nTx Scott\n________________________________\nDe : scottaohara ***@***.***>\nEnvoyé : 27 octobre 2022 08:49\nÀ : whatwg/html ***@***.***>\nCc : Oznogco ***@***.***>; Mention ***@***.***>\nObjet : Re: [whatwg/html] \"Here are some examples of valid headings contai...\" (Issue #8438)\n\n\n@Oznogco<https://github.com/Oznogco> there is already a bug for the validator to output the updated information: validator/validator#1397<https://github.com/validator/validator/issues/1397>\n\nthe validator is presently incorrect, not the HTML spec.\n\n—\nReply to this email directly, view it on GitHub<https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/8438#issuecomment-1293478139>, or unsubscribe<https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AG3ZPWEZUOI3C5KJUXTHIM3WFJ25LANCNFSM6AAAAAARPPI4CU>.\nYou are receiving this because you were mentioned.Message ID: ***@***.***>\n",
